   "source": [
    "# Idea 8 of the ideas planner, step 1: can polarity and blur be read from the photo and the map at the chosen place?\n",
    "Facts found first: the coarse stage's edge bins are already UNSIGNED (angle mod pi in `edge_features.gradient_parts`), so a polarity flip cannot hurt the coarse correlation; the loss of an inverted photo (Test_Iteration_9: official 48.8 -> 35.4) sits in the stages after it (DINO tokens, LoFTR). Blur 2 px costs 29 points on the official photos and nothing on NUDT.\n",
    "Estimators (no learning): at the top peak of the first standard query (and at the truth, to separate estimator error from localisation error) cut the map window, then\n",
    " polarity = cosine of the signed gradients of canvas and window over the valid pixels (negative = opposite polarity);\n",
    " blur = ratio of the mean gradient magnitude, canvas over window (well below 1 = the photo is blurrier than the map).\n",
    "The same 60 official photos as Test_Iteration_9; kinds clean, invert, blur (the same perturbation function). Reading: the idea needs the polarity sign to separate inverted from clean, and the gradient ratio to separate blurred from clean, on most photos; otherwise step 2 (end to end) is not worth running.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "31e4947a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os, sys, time\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "ROOT = Path.cwd()\n",
    "while not (ROOT / \"single_photo_pipeline.py\").exists():\n",
    "    ROOT = ROOT.parent\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT)); sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / \"src\")); os.chdir(ROOT)\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA = os.environ.get(\"GATE_DATA\", \"official\")\n",
    "MAP = \"new\"\n",
    "POOL_PHOTOS = int(os.environ.get(\"POOL_PHOTOS\", \"500\"))   # same pool and setup seed as Test_Iteration_3, so NUDT seed 101 / 202 pick the same photos\n",
    "WIDE_HEADINGS = [-10.0, -7.5, -5.0, -2.5, 0.0, 2.5, 5.0, 7.5, 10.0]\n",
    "WIDE_SCALES = [0.95, 1.0, 1.05]\n",
    "K_PER_QUERY, M_PER_QUERY = 50, 10\n",
    "MATCHER_CONFIDENCE, LOFTR_COARSE_THRESHOLD = 0.22, 0.21\n",
    "MIN_INLIERS, GAMMA = 8, 1.0\n",
    "NUDT_SEED = int(os.environ.get(\"NUDT_SEED\", \"101\"))\n",
    "N_NUDT = int(os.environ.get(\"N_NUDT\", \"300\"))\n",
    "EXCLUDE_SEEDS = [int(s) for s in os.environ.get(\"EXCLUDE_SEEDS\", \"\").split(\",\") if s.strip()]\n",
    "N_LIMIT = int(os.environ.get(\"N_LIMIT\", \"0\"))\n",
    "EXCLUDE_N = int(os.environ.get(\"EXCLUDE_N\", \"300\"))   # size of the excluded seeds' samples (seed 101 picked 300; this reproduces Test_Iteration_3's seed 202 photos exactly)\n",
    "MATCHER = os.environ.get(\"MATCHER\", \"loftr\")          # \"loftr\" (the pipeline) or \"xoftr\" (MINIMA XoFTR, a swap-in with the same plumbing)\n",
    "XOFTR_COARSE, XOFTR_FINE = float(os.environ.get(\"XOFTR_COARSE\", \"0.3\")), float(os.environ.get(\"XOFTR_FINE\", \"0.1\"))\n",
    "FRESH_EXCLUDE_POOL = int(os.environ.get(\"FRESH_EXCLUDE_POOL\", \"0\"))   # >0 (NUDT, with POOL_PHOTOS >= all frames): skip every photo of the usual\n",
    "# pool of this size (setup seed 7), so the sample is from photos no earlier test has used\n",
    "EXCLUDE_IDS_FILE = os.environ.get(\"EXCLUDE_IDS_FILE\")   # optional csv with a photo column: never draw these photos (an earlier fresh sample)\n",
    "PHOTOS_FILE = os.environ.get(\"PHOTOS_FILE\")           # optional csv with a photo column: only these photos\n",
    "print(MATCHER, DATA, \"seed\", NUDT_SEED, \"n\", N_NUDT, \"exclude\", EXCLUDE_SEEDS, \"limit\", N_LIMIT)"
   ]
